      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable that you feel this way when everything feels shattered, and the idea of \"navigating\" something that feels permanently lost is terrifying. Sometimes, the profound sense of loss is the most real thing in the room, and it deserves to be acknowledged as such. While the weight feels absolute, even the most broken things can find a new, quiet form of existence. Consider finding a support group where people share similar, deep-seated struggles; sometimes, shared experience is the only thing that truly \"gets it.\"",
